\pard\plain \ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0 \bullet \~}{\f0\fs24\b1 What\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s the main character\u8217\'92s internal conflict?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~In most novels, this is a question that gets answered early in the outlining process, since it will drive the entirety of the story}{\f0\fs24\b0\i1 .}{\f0\fs24\b0 \line \bullet \~}{\f0\fs24\b1 Which of the main character\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s views will change as a result of the story\u8217\'92s events?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~}{\f0\fs24\b1 How and why?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~This is where you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92ll find the underlying force of your theme. Your}{ }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 character\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s views will define his actions, and his actions will define the story.\line \bullet \~}{\f0\fs24\b1 How will the main character demonstrate his respective views and attitudes at the beginning and the end of the story?\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 This is an extension of the previous question, but it is vital because, as we discussed earlier in regard to character arc, its answer will prove the changes to the reader.\line \bullet \~}{\f0\fs24\b1 Is there any particular symbolism that can reinforce the theme and the character\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s attitude toward it?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~Like theme itself, symbolism is often overstated and generally better when culled organically from your unconscious mind. For example, sometimes you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92ll find yourself using a particular color or image to represent something. If the symbol proves effective, you can later go back and strengthen it. (Refer to the section \u8220\'93}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "javascript:void(0)"}{\fldrslt\f0\fs24\b0 How to Strengthen Your Theme With Symbolism}}{\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 on the following page.)\line \bullet \~}{\f0\fs24\b1 How can you use the subtext (the unstated) to exemplify the theme, so you won\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t have to spell it out for the reader?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~When it comes to theme, the unstated is almost always more powerful than the direct. In real life, when we find ourselves learning lessons and changing views, we can\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t always immediately define the changes in precise language. And neither should your character. Lord Jim didn\u8217\'92t have to\~}{\f0\fs24\b0\i1 tell\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 us his actions on the island were a direct result of his earlier cowardice; the connection was obvious from the subtext and would, in fact, have weakened if Conrad mentioned it outright.}{ }
