\par\plain {EX: }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b1 Weakness}{\f0\fs24\b0 : Chris Redston is selfish and irresponsible: He spends his life in search of the next big adrenaline trip, not really caring whom he lets down or hurts along the way.\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 Who is he hurting?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~His dad, Joe, random bystanders, Brooke, Lisa, Mike.\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 What does this character want?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~Chris wants to make the dreams stop.\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 What does this character need?\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 To take responsibility for his actions and sacrifice himself for the good of others.\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 What does he know at the beginning?\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 That people shirk their responsibilities and hurt you, and that life is always just one step away from catastrophe, so you might as well live it to the hilt. Excitement kills the pain and proves you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re still alive. If you never act responsible, then no one will expect you to be responsible, or be hurt when you fail to be responsible. (His fear of injuring others is buried deep in his unstated psyche. He would never\~}{\f0\fs24\b0\i1 tell}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~you that.)\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 What is he\~}{\f0\fs24\b1\i1 wrong}{\f0\fs24\b1 \~about in the beginning?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~He thinks the best way to avoid hurting people is to avoid responsibility. He thinks the only way to feel alive is to risk his life.\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 What will he learn at the end?}{\f0\fs24\b0 \~To take responsibility for his actions and act for others above himself.\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 Hero\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s central problem}{\f0\fs24\b0 : The realization that taking responsibility isn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t just a flippant decision; sometimes it\u8217\'92s a soul-deep commitment.\~\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 Thematic principle}{\f0\fs24\b0 : Force an irresponsible young man to learn responsibility when his actions endanger two worlds.\line }{\f0\fs24\b1 Theme:\~}{\f0\fs24\b0 If you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re going to succeed as a human being, you have to take responsibility for your actions, even if it means losing what you love most.}{ }}